WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.560
A tree with no leaves in winter is not dead.

2
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.780
It is resting. Visit one tree all year, watch the seasons come in the same order,

3
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.760
and find the buds already holding next spring's leaves.

4
00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:20.893
You need one tree that loses its leaves in fall, one you can reach safely and have

5
00:00:20.893 --> 00:00:21.893
permission to visit.

6
00:00:22.693 --> 00:00:24.253
Bring a phone or camera and paper.

7
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:29.117
Stand ten to twenty steps back, so the whole tree fits in the photo.

8
00:00:29.857 --> 00:00:33.617
Pick a landmark, and take every photo from there, facing the same way.

9
00:00:34.377 --> 00:00:35.477
Your child predicts first.

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.920
Visit about once a month for fifteen minutes.

11
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.540
Notice the weather and look for animals.

12
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.760
In much of Virginia, buds swell and open in March and April.

13
00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:50.240
Dates vary. Compare each new photo with the last one.

14
00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:54.740
A bare winter twig still has buds, so the tree is resting, not dead.

15
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:58.263
Stay with your child at the tree on every visit.

16
00:00:59.223 --> 00:01:03.103
Feet stay on the ground, with no climbing, and nothing from the tree goes in a

17
00:01:03.103 --> 00:01:03.303
mouth.
